[Music]  you guys might be wondering why it's  been so long since we uploaded something  to the main channel well we've been  shooting something called sync for the  past two months sync is a web series  we've been working on and if you haven't  seen it check it out it's a huge 12  episode web series and it's nuts you  guys have been asking for a bigger  project from us so here it is anyways  now that we're all done shooting it it's  off in the hands of editors music guys  sound guys we have a lot more free time  now now that we're not shooting it  anymore so you guys can look forward to  a video every two weeks just like the  good old days until the end of time  until  we get killed until the internet is shut  down by old men who don't understand  youtube so i bet you guys are wondering  how did we come up with the idea for  this crazy video well we're actually  working on another video unfortunately  things started falling apart we realized  wait a second we need to make a video  right now at the last second we only got  a couple hours so we took a look at what  we had we realized wait a second you can  do motion capture with an xbox connect  so we took that idea when we ran with it  and we started doing some animation  tests started getting some little dance  animations and they're so funny that we  realized wait a second  we have to make a whole video just about  us dancing as miniature figurines after  going out to the warehouse and dancing  around and staring at nothingness with  our cg goggles  we came back and started the process for  this video  one really cool thing about it is that  pretty much the entire the entire effect  is done with an automated process uh we  start with the connect and we  automatically get motion capture data  for our actual dance moves and then we  move on to our bodies which we created  using a program called one two three d  catch terrible name great program but uh  we used that to construct a 3d model  based off of composite images that we  took in a 360 degree circle of ourselves  and then for our faces and face models  we used a program called face gen which  will automatically create a  very similar looking 3d model of your  face based off of three photos it's not  perfect but it gets the job done no hair  though so kind of have to do this one  bald and the face gen heads comes with  something comes with something called a  morph target where uh basically gives  you all the different expressions and  you can link those to the model and then  you just mark between them to get your  different facial expressions so that's  how i made little munchkin guys going  and stuff oh here's something cool  there's one shot when the whole group of  guys begin to dance believe it or not  that shot is 100 cg there's not a real  element in that shot even though it  looks like a real concrete floor and  real people in the background it is  entirely virtual  so for those of you guys out there who  want to try to do the same thing  basically plug your connect into your  computer uh there's a program that we  use called reckle connect um basically  you load that up record your animation  you save it out as a bvh file which is  like a universal motion capture file in  3ds max you create a biped and you can  load that as motion capture data on the  biped that's basically all there is to  it um there's some small nuances here  and there if you just you know mess  around with it you'll probably figure it  out  you guys are always welcome to tweet at  us with any questions if you're trying  it out at corridor digital so good luck  you

